Data sources (P1/S8 ObservableObject VM → generated C# client, web hook names kept at the C# call sites):
  useVehicles (GET /vehicles)               -> CommandsSource.FetchAsync step 1, ApiRequest(Operations.Vehicles.List)
  command-vehicle-states (per-vehicle       -> CommandsSource.FetchAsync step 2, ApiRequest(Operations.Vehicles.State, vehicleID),
    GET /vehicles/{vehicleID}/state)            per-vehicle try/catch → null (web catch → null); systemic outage → StatesError
  The manifest declares no dataSources for this page (the web page reads inline request() rather than a named
  hook), so the generator saw none; the real reads are still ported in full — no scope narrowing.
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API; converted only at the display boundary in CommandsProjection.Center via
  UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi (rated_range metres) + UnitConverters.TemperatureFromSi (inside_temp °C) +
  ScalarFormatters/UnitLabels (no non-SI stored/computed).
Live data: web uses TanStack-Query polling (refetchInterval 15_000), not useLiveX/SSE — reproduced with a
  DispatcherTimer(15s) → ViewModel.RefreshAsync in CommandsPage.cs (no SSE subscription / staleness chip; the
  per-vehicle freshness is shown by TsFreshnessIndicator over updated_at, the 2-min contract).
Scope note: the per-vehicle interactive command catalogue (search / favourites / category tiles) is delivered
  by the separately-tracked CommandTile / CommandSearch / CollapsibleCommandGroup parity units; this page
  reproduces the VehicleCommandCenter header region (identity + state badge + freshness + model·vin + the live
  battery / range / temperature readouts) so the success state renders one centre per roster vehicle. The
  manifest's panels for this unit are the 4 stat MetricCards + the statesError GlassPanel only.

